# Project memory

This repo’s durable knowledge lives under [`memory/`](memory/). Prefer it over inventing process from scratch.

## Read first

| Path | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `memory/roles/` | AAC role briefs and review/merge contracts |
| `memory/skills/` | Reusable skills and playbooks |
| `memory/lessons/` | Distilled experience from real runs (what worked, what failed, what to avoid) |

When the task touches orchestration, specs, review, or agent workflow, check the matching files under `memory/` before changing prompts or scripts.

## Write lasting knowledge here

If you learn something worth reusing—failed approaches, prompt/review pitfalls, dogfood gotchas, operational conventions—**record it under `memory/`**, usually as a short note in `memory/lessons/`.

- Prefer small, dated or topic-named markdown files (e.g. `memory/lessons/spec-brevity.md`).
- Update an existing role/skill when the lesson belongs there; do not only leave it in chat.
- Do not dump raw run logs; distill into actionable guidance.
- Transient run artifacts stay in `aac/` / `artifacts/`; they are not memory.
